invariant: INV-17
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh srv_tcp_nonblocking
reason: tcp_nonblocking_fail marks the session dead and does not wipe it,
  so a failed tcp-nonblocking session keeps its traffic keys and
  handshake secrets. The driver's proof asserts that every failure of
  ch_srv_record_in leaves no secret, and fails on this edit.

--- old
    r->t.alert_sent = alert;
    tcp_nonblocking_wipe(r);
    r->t.state = CH_ST_FAILED;
--- new
    r->t.alert_sent = alert;
    r->t.state = CH_ST_FAILED;
